<section class="about" id="about">
<h2 data-i18n="t1">about</h2>
<p data-i18n="t5">I study computational technologies and the philosophies they manufacture. I am particularly interested in machine translation and virtual private networks, among other technologies that help us map alternative geographies and question the limits of representation.</p>
<p data-i18n="t6">As a <a href="https://fondazionealfonsocoin.it/news#c10619">Fondazione Alfonso Coin</a> scholar, I study Digital and Public Humanities at VeDPH, Ca’ Foscari University of Venice, living and working in one of the major centers of early modern technological innovation.</p>
<p data-i18n="t7">Beyond media studies, my professional interests include UX/UI writing and educational policymaking. In my free time, I enjoy painting, especially still life.</p>
<p data-i18n="t46">I am always interested in collaborating—or even just chatting: feel free to <a href="mailto:nvvnb@proton.me">get in touch</a>!</p>
</section>
